<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore January M1 rises 9.9 pct on year - MAS.</title>
<headline>Singapore January M1 rises 9.9 pct on year - MAS.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Money supply figures.</p>
<p>	   (in billions of Singapore dollars)</p>
<p>				  Jan	Dec    Jan'96</p>
<p>M-1 (narrow money)	 28.85   27.04     26.24</p>
<p>M-2			   113.06  111.95    101.80</p>
<p>M-3 (broad money)	 141.70  139.84    128.16</p>
<p>Demand deposits	    17.84   16.75     16.50</p>
<p>Currency in active	 11.01   10.29	9.73</p>
<p>circulation  </p>
<p>Note - The Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS) said narrow money supply (M1) grew by 9.9 percent year-on-year in January, compared with 6.7 percent in December.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703080)</p>
</text>
